@page "/mud/project/sponsor"

<DocsPage DisplayFooter="true">
    <DocsPageHeader Title="Sponsors & Backers" SubTitle="The continued development and maintenance of ProtonBlazor is secured by our sponsors"/>
    <DocsPageContent>

        <DocsPageSection>
            <SectionHeader Title="Sponsor">
                <Description>
                    ProtonBlazor is open-source because we want to include the community in the project and influence what direction we are heading. While ProtonBlazor is entirely free to use and always will be, we have a lot of contributors and a core team that invests a lot of time into the project.
                    We want to make sure ProtonBlazor becomes a financially stable project. That is why we have gone with the crowd-funding concept to invest in infrastructure, possible dev payouts, and potentially full-time devs in the future.<br/><br/>
                    By supporting us, you help secure the continued development and maintenance of ProtonBlazor, that bugs get fixed, new features get implemented, support for coming versions of .NET and Blazor.
                </Description>
            </SectionHeader>
            
            <SectionSubGroups>
                <DocsPageSection>
                    <SectionHeader Title="Become a sponsor">
                        <Description>
                            <ProButton DropShadow="false" StartIcon="@Icons.Material.Filled.DataUsage" IconColor="Color.Info" Size="Size.Large" Variant="Variant.Filled" Class="docs-no-text-transform" Href="https://opencollective.com/protonblazor" Target="_blank">Sponsor on Open Collective</ProButton>
                        </Description>
                    </SectionHeader>
                </DocsPageSection>

                <DocsPageSection>
                    <SectionHeader Title="Sponsor Individuals">
                        <Description>
                            This is a great way to directly support the developers behind the library and recognize their ongoing efforts in maintaining and improving the project.<br/>
                            Check the <ProLink Href="/mud/project/team">Team & Contributors</ProLink> page for individual sponsorship options.<br/>
                        </Description>
                    </SectionHeader>
                </DocsPageSection>

                <DocsPageSection>
                    <SectionHeader Title="What we do">
                        <Description>
                            <div class="d-flex flex-column px-2">
                                <ProBadge Class="mt-1" Color="Color.Primary" Dot="true" Origin="Origin.CenterLeft">
                                    <div class="pl-4 docs-line-height-normal">
                                        Oversee the library as a whole
                                    </div>
                                </ProBadge>
                                <ProBadge Class="mt-1" Color="Color.Primary" Dot="true" Origin="Origin.CenterLeft">
                                    <div class="pl-4 docs-line-height-normal">
                                        Planning features and deciding which ones should be implemented and which should not
                                    </div>
                                </ProBadge>
                                <ProBadge Class="mt-1" Color="Color.Primary" Dot="true" Origin="Origin.CenterLeft">
                                    <div class="pl-4 docs-line-height-normal">
                                        Develop new features and ideas
                                    </div>
                                </ProBadge>
                                <ProBadge Class="mt-1" Color="Color.Primary" Dot="true" Origin="Origin.CenterLeft">
                                    <div class="pl-4 docs-line-height-normal">
                                        Fix reported bugs
                                    </div>
                                </ProBadge>
                                <ProBadge Class="mt-1" Color="Color.Primary" Dot="true" Origin="Origin.CenterLeft">
                                    <div class="pl-4 docs-line-height-normal">
                                        Write new documentation and improve on old
                                    </div>
                                </ProBadge>
                                <ProBadge Class="mt-1" Color="Color.Primary" Dot="true" Origin="Origin.CenterLeft">
                                    <div class="pl-4 docs-line-height-normal">
                                        Adopt new versions of .NET and Blazor
                                    </div>
                                </ProBadge>
                                <ProBadge Class="mt-1" Color="Color.Primary" Dot="true" Origin="Origin.CenterLeft">
                                    <div class="pl-4 docs-line-height-normal">
                                        QA, creating tests or manually testing
                                    </div>
                                </ProBadge>
                                <ProBadge Class="mt-1" Color="Color.Primary" Dot="true" Origin="Origin.CenterLeft">
                                    <div class="pl-4 docs-line-height-normal">
                                        Manage Issues/Feature Requests/Discussions/Pull Requests/Reviews on GitHub
                                    </div>
                                </ProBadge>
                                <ProBadge Class="mt-1" Color="Color.Primary" Dot="true" Origin="Origin.CenterLeft">
                                    <div class="pl-4 docs-line-height-normal">
                                        CI/CD workflows to ensure continuous delivery/deployment
                                    </div>
                                </ProBadge>
                                <ProBadge Class="mt-1" Color="Color.Primary" Dot="true" Origin="Origin.CenterLeft">
                                    <div class="pl-4 docs-line-height-normal">
                                        Community building, e.g., Reddit, Twitter, Stack Overflow, Discord
                                    </div>
                                </ProBadge>
                            </div>
                        </Description>
                    </SectionHeader>
                </DocsPageSection>

                <DocsPageSection>
                    <SectionHeader Title="What's the difference between sponsoring via Open Collective and GitHub?">
                        <Description>
                            Funds received via <b>Open Collective</b> are managed transparently and aimed to sustain ProtonBlazor and its needs.<br/>
                            As a
                            <ProTooltip Color="Color.Dark" Placement="Placement.Top">
                                <ChildContent>
                                    <ProText Class="docs-text-dec">Fiscal Host</ProText>
                                </ChildContent>
                                <TooltipContent>
                                    A Fiscal Host is an entity that holds the money on<br/>
                                    behalf of a Collective and takes care of<br/>
                                    accounting, taxes, and invoices.
                                </TooltipContent>
                            </ProTooltip>, all funds are kept there until we submit an expense.<br/><br/>
                            Funds received via <b>GitHub</b>, directly go to <CodeInline>Gardnet AB</CodeInline> which is a Swedish company owned by <ProLink Href="https://github.com/Garderoben">Garderoben</ProLink>, the creator of ProtonBlazor. The company is a profit entity with one goal, to secure ProtonBlazor's future.
                        </Description>
                    </SectionHeader>
                </DocsPageSection>

            </SectionSubGroups>
        </DocsPageSection>

